00:28:52,220 --> 00:28:54,300
related to the cost of capital.

482
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:55,980
That can be very prohibitive.

483
00:28:55,980 --> 00:29:01,460
And when you look at, for example, capital adequacy, the UK and European and

484
00:29:01,460 --> 00:29:05,540
traditional financial markets have fairly long equations for how you come up with

485
00:29:05,540 --> 00:29:06,340
capital adequacy.

486
00:29:06,340 --> 00:29:09,420
The US typically has a more straightforward program.

487
00:29:09,420 --> 00:29:11,300
So that's something to keep an eye on.

488
00:29:11,300 --> 00:29:14,860
I think the two things I would say for this is that, again, championing the idea

