00:36:55,780 --> 00:37:00,260
And so what we look at when we think about who is the best price,

630
00:37:00,260 --> 00:37:04,340
how do you get the bid in the offer, we look at price, size and time.

631
00:37:04,340 --> 00:37:09,340
This is normal. This is what most exchanges and venues would look at.

632
00:37:09,340 --> 00:37:14,060
But now what we can do is we can overlay the historical data of fill ratio,

633
00:37:14,060 --> 00:37:19,340
response times and market impact of the market maker in real time.

634
00:37:19,340 --> 00:37:22,620
So, for example, if you come and you're top of book,

635
00:37:22,620 --> 00:37:26,740
but your response time is very low or we see that you're not filling trades

636
00:37:26,740 --> 00:37:29,500
as much as we would like, there's a real cost to that.

637
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:33,060
So the cost to your price is actually worse than what you're showing.

638
00:37:33,060 --> 00:37:36,620
And what our system does is automatically account for that.

639
00:37:36,660 --> 00:37:40,900
Where we get the home run ball out of this is we operate right now

640
00:37:40,900 --> 00:37:46,860
environmental in Equinix LD4 in London, in Equinix NY4 in New York.

641
00:37:46,860 --> 00:37:49,420
We're also currently in the cloud in AWS Tokyo.

642
00:37:49,420 --> 00:37:54,780
And later this year, we'll look to go into either TY3 in Tokyo or SG3.

643
00:37:54,780 --> 00:37:57,260
When you do that, this is true in every other market,

644
00:37:57,260 --> 00:38:01,380
when you have multiple matching engines, they are independent of one another.

645
00:38:01,380 --> 00:38:06,180
And so they have independent liquidity and no one has ever tied these things

646
00:38:06,180 --> 00:38:09,300
together in financial markets. We're hoping to be the first.

647
00:38:09,300 --> 00:38:13,060
Our CTO, our third co-founder, Vlad Ryzen, who's a double PhD in math

648
00:38:13,060 --> 00:38:17,900
and artificial intelligence, we're going to use AI to basically combine

649
00:38:17,900 --> 00:38:21,340
all the matching engines to have one global matching engine.

650
00:38:21,340 --> 00:38:26,380
And so the relationship here is if you look at something, for example,

651
00:38:26,380 --> 00:38:32,100
like response times, the latency between New York and London is around 70 to 120

652
00:38:32,100 --> 00:38:35,380
milliseconds, not lower, not higher.

653
00:38:35,420 --> 00:38:38,140
We know that it's pretty static over time.

654
00:38:38,140 --> 00:38:42,220
And so if you know this mathematically, then you can adjust.

655
00:38:42,220 --> 00:38:47,500
You can imagine there are moments in time where a taker in our US engine

656
00:38:47,500 --> 00:38:51,220
might be better matched with a market maker from our London engine.

657
00:38:51,220 --> 00:38:56,300
Having this SOR overlay under our best execution allows us to eventually

658
00:38:56,300 --> 00:39:02,700
embed AI to combine all of our liquidity globally as well as the customer's credit.

659
00:39:02,700 --> 00:39:04,340
So we think that's going to be a home run.

